- Mobile First Shell: `kc-ui` now boots into a mobile-first home shell with visible gallery and commission sections so the two core product directions are represented from the first scaffold.
- Metadata Gallery Feed: `kc-ui` now loads published gallery records from `kc-api`, rendering real image/title/description cards from database-backed metadata instead of hardcoded placeholders.
- Profile Admin Gallery: signed-in users now have profile pages, and Kyra can use an admin tools accordion on her profile to upload, create, edit, delete, and drag-drop reorder gallery items.
- Anonymous Order Slice: customers can now submit commission orders with reference images, open shared 6-digit order pages, comment on orders, review quote/payment status, and Kyra can manage categories, quotes, statuses, and paginated orders from the admin profile.
- Direct Admin Route: admin sign-in now lives on direct `/admin` routes, with no public sign-in button in the app nav and cleaner admin-only route handling.
- Manual Order Acceptance: Kyra can now mark an order accepted from admin controls for off-app payments like Venmo, as long as the order has a saved quote.
- Submission Link Email: customers now get an email with their order number and direct order link right after a successful commission submission when mail is configured.
- Accordion Admin Tools: Kyra's profile now splits admin work into separate gallery-creation, edit-gallery, and category accordions, with responsive gallery management cards and visible drag handles.
- Save Time Gallery: gallery item images now stay local until the admin saves the item, while still showing an immediate local preview and avoiding abandoned draft uploads to S3.
- Automatic Comment Emails: new customer and admin comments now email the other side immediately with a direct anchor link to the new comment, while edited comments stay in-app only.
- Priced Gallery Checkout: gallery items can now carry an optional sale price, show a buy button on the homepage, go through Stripe Checkout with shipping collection, and land as paid gallery orders in Kyra's All Orders list.
- Shared Gallery Orders: paid gallery purchases now open on the shared order route with artwork preview, shipping details, payment-processing handling, customer order-link email, and admin shipment status controls.
- Confirmed Gallery Deletes: Kyra now has to confirm gallery deletions from Edit Gallery before an artwork is removed, with an inline cancel path on the selected card.
- Autosaved Gallery Order: Kyra's gallery reorder changes now save automatically as soon as she drops an artwork into its new position.
- Required Service Fields: the commission request form now requires name, email, phone, service, instructions, medium, and size before an order can be submitted.
- Service Copy Refresh: user-facing commission copy now says service/services instead of category/categories across the active app flow.
- Gallery Inquiry Orders: priced gallery items now support ask-a-question inquiries with their own order page, shared comments thread, artwork preview, and checkout handoff.
- Paid Order Comments: paid gallery orders now support the same shared customer/admin comments thread as commission orders, with edit/delete and new-comment email behavior.
- Delivery Receipt Check: delivered commission and paid gallery orders now let the customer confirm receipt from the shared order page with a simple yes/no confirmation step.
- Status Update Emails: customers now get an automatic email each time admin changes an order status, including quote, decline, acceptance, progress, shipment, and delivery changes.
- Inquiry Order Labels: Kyra's `All Orders` list now clearly labels gallery inquiry rows so unpaid artwork questions are visible before checkout.
- Receipt Status Checkmarks: customer-confirmed delivered orders now show a small green checkmark in Kyra's `All Orders` cards and on the shared order page.
